f.d:
Precious guru, unified essence of all buddhas of the three times:
Outwardly I offer flowers and incense;
inwardly, five meats and five elixirs;
secretly, the timeless awareness of bliss-emptiness;
and most secretly, the sublime offering of suchness.
Please accept and confer the complete four empowerments.

Visualize the guru and seat as before. Imagine that you present the four complete and perfect offerings: the outer offerings of manifold excellent substances and offerings from all times and directions; the inner offerings of sacred pledge and elixir of awareness; {217} the secret offering of a bliss-inducing wisdom consort; and the suchness offering of knowing that the three spheres are like an illusion and a dream.
Precious guru, unified essence of all buddhas of the three times:
Outwardly I offer flowers and incense;
inwardly, five meats and five elixirs;
secretly, the timeless awareness of bliss-emptiness;
and most secretly, the sublime offering of suchness.
Please accept and confer the complete four empowerments.

For a short, general version:
Precious guru, unified essence of all buddhas of the three times:
Outwardly I offer flowers and incense;
inwardly, five meats and five elixirs;
secretly, the timeless awareness of bliss-emptiness;
and most secretly, the sublime offering of suchness.
Accept them and purify all violations of my sacred pledge.
Please grant me the supreme spiritual power of mahāmudrā on this very seat. {256}

hūṃ hūṃ phaṭ
Also do the one verse praise:
Glorious Vajra Ḍākinī,
[wheel wielder of the ḍākinīs
with fivefold awareness and three kāyas;
homage to the protector of migrators.] {267}

I present vast clouds of outer, inner, and secret offerings;
sincerely confess every individual fault;
rejoice; request the turning of the dharma wheel;
supplicate you to remain always; and dedicate this to awakening.

Your kunda radiates there, {294}
increases in the mother,
red complexion grows on the white;
the mother overpowers the father.

Through that, all stains of attachment
to deity’s form mahāmudrā are purified;
free, self-arising purity arises.

Kunzang Chöjor, Lozang Tutop,
Nyima Chöpel, Losal Tenkyong,
Khyentse Wangpo, the real Mañjuśrī. {299}

Since this is the special [method for] maturation, the person who would ripen their being and train with the four contemplations that turn the mind should sit on a comfortable seat in an isolated place with the [physical] positions of meditative stability. In the space before you is a jeweled throne supported by eight great lions, upon which is a seat of a multicolored lotus, sun, and moon. On that is your root guru, the epitome of the awakened body, speech, mind, and the vajra awareness of all buddhas. The guru’s form is incomparably charismatic, smiling slightly, resting in the equipoise of numerous approaches to meditative absorption. If just hearing the guru’s name liberates from cyclic existence and the lower realms, what is there to say about supplicating for whatever your exigencies? Imagine that you and all sentient beings headed by your parents go for refuge all together. Say:
All sentient beings, my mothers, equal to the reaches of space, go for refuge in the precious guru, the unified essence of all refuges. {301}
Repeat that seven or more times.

That is the actual saṃbhogakāya.
The (third), nail of four classes of ḍākinī in the navel:
The light of A burns;
if you practice threefold nonabiding (of body, speech, and mind),
you accomplish the supreme and common in years and months.

The (mother’s color is) white with a red radiance;
the mother is controlled by the father.
Thus the couple is shaken by light. {328}
When your being is filled with bliss,
the forceful contracting of the lower wind
and the meaning of emptiness is revealed by bliss.

I supplicate Ngawang Tenpa Rabgye
at the secluded place of Secret Mantra Great Bliss. {332}
…

I supplicate Jalu Gönpo Paljor
in the pure realm of Khecara, site of lucid clarity. {334}
…

Vajradhara, pervading lord of everything;
Niguma, secret sublime delight;
Khyungpo Yogi, with five culminations;
Mokchokpa, king of supreme spiritual power;

Öntön Kyergangpa, bodhisattva at the stream’s end;
Nyentönpa, dancer in illusion’s integral unity;
Lord Tönpa, gone to buddhahood in one lifetime;
Tsangma Shangtön Tsultrim Bumpa, the honorable;

Zhönu Drup, sealed by the awareness mudra;
Gyaltsen Bum, the desired learned righteous adept;
Tsultrim Gön, desired emanation in existence;
Rechenpa, blazing with the brilliance of sublime caṇḍālī;

Rin Gyalwa [Shangpa Karpo], drenched in illusion’s elixir;
Sangye Pal, accomplisher of wind-mind as deity’s form;
Namkha Gyal, illuminated by the light of bliss-emptiness;
Lekpa Gyal[tsen], appearance dissolved into native mind;

[Kunga] Drolchok, lord of the Vajra Queen;
Chöku Lhawang Drak, full of undissipating bliss;
Drolwai Gönpo, glorious secret heruka;
[Yeshe] Gyatso, regent of embodied awareness;

[Jampa] Yönten Gön, taking up deliberate conduct on the path;
Gönpo Paljor, gone in a rainbow body;
Gönpo Drakpa, equalizer of samsara and nirvana;
[Gönpo] Namgyal, intoxicated by coemergent joy;

Rikdzin [Tsewang Norbu], leader of a million learned adepts;
[Kagyu] Trinle Shingta, real holder of the white lotus;
[Kunga Gelek] Palbar, a hundred lights of virtue and realization;
Kunga Lhundrup [Gyatso], treasure revealer of abiding nature;

[Ngawang] Lodröpa, always guided by beautiful Khecarī;
Lord Karma Lhaktong, hidden buddha;
Zhenpen Özer, receiver of wind-mind empowerment;
my root guru, holder of the treasury of instructions:

I obtain the fourth empowerment; all blessings are perfectly complete.
The source of phenomena dissipates in light; the guru dissolves into me;
my three doors become inseparable from the three vajras. {341}

Filling all space: I offer to the guru and deities.
Goddesses in perfect rapture of luminous illusory supreme bliss,
with lutes, flutes, kettle drums, and clay drums;
goddesses of laughter, charm, song, and dance;

goddesses of fine flowers, incense, light, and perfume;
goddesses of form, taste, touch, and source of phenomena:
sixteen goddesses with aspects of joy perfectly complete.
May this display by the vajra consort’s joy {368}
please your vajra mind, Heruka.

Wish-granting cows, source of desires;
crops that grow without cultivation;
wish-fulfilling trees; supreme fruits;
and excellent vases: filling all space, I offer.

Food of the five elixirs,
the very stuff of spiritual powers;
supreme food of the five lamps,
the principal pledge of all buddhas;

Not dependent on the aggregates,
constituents, and sense fields;
completely free of misapprehensions:
homage and praise to you, the inconceivable. {370}

May I never displease the guru,
for there is no other victorious one,
but be able to achieve only their pleasure {379}
by rendering all manner of service with three doors.

I offer my virtue, body, and possessions in three times,
without any clinging to the offering substances, {381}
and my practice of prayer, mantra, mudra, and meditation;
I present all outer, inner, and secret offerings.

Bereft of the guru, I will not succeed
in practices of mantra and mudra;
I supplicate you to not transcend misery.

Precious one, source of the mind’s desires,
lord protector, this is my request to you:
let the Buddha’s Holy Dharma, source of benefit and happiness,
flourish through study, contemplation, and practice. {384}

Qualities fully perfected like the snow mountains,
from which blessing rivers quench fortunate disciples,
you who reveal my mind as coemergence;
may there be auspiciousness of the sublime gurus, dharma sovereigns.

In the daytime, inconceivable, inexpressible mahāmudrā;
in the nighttime, spontaneous lucid clarity with three aspects;
self-arising nature of integral unity arose—
you perfected the victors’ three kāyas; I supplicate you.

The flower of your marks and signs smells of the three trainings;
the stamens of knowledge and love are your flawless beautiful form;
seeing, hearing, or recalling you relieves longing—
Shangtönpa Khedrup Chöje, I supplicate you.

You supplicated Sangye Tönpa on the road to meet him
and experienced meditative absorption in illusion and dreams;
just by seeing his face your conceptual patterns
were liberated in dharmakāya; I supplicate you. {419}

Once you manifested the form of the yidam deity;
sometimes the heroes and ḍākinīs rendered service;
the nine great beings bowed and obeyed you—
public lord of adepts, I supplicate you.

Your three secrets immaculate, the golden mountain;
your dharma robes between sessions shrouding it in red light;
your higher trainings, the sun and moon mandalas,
dispelling the darkness of the three realms; I supplicate you.

Grasping with mind-made effort vanished in basic space;
deluded thoughts of ordinary attachment subsided in their own ground;
within the great infinite purity of whatever appeared,
the wheel of timeless awareness arose; I supplicate you.

Externally, may the cave of eight worldly deceptions collapse;
internally, may the light of the unchanging bliss of melting blaze;
secretly, may I directly see the dharmakāya beyond concepts;
and may I quickly achieve the liberated life of Nyame Sangye.

In one day of study, your confidence arose from within;
in one month of yoga, you became adept; in one year, you had arrived;
in one lifetime, you taught and practiced as a buddha—
such praise pervaded the earth, I supplicate you.

While doing your practice at Tarpa Ling, {433}
you actually met Great Vajradhara with the five-family buddhas,
the eight bodhisattvas, the ten wrathful ones, and the [five] goddesses;
you received the profound path and many other profound teachings—
free of the darkness of two obscurations, I supplicate you.

In outward manner, you were bound by the training of pure prātimokṣa;
inwardly, you had perfect control of the mind of awakening;
secretly, you upheld the deliberate behavior of Mantra—
sublime sovereign, I supplicate you.

You provided disciples with training supports without bias
from the great chariot of the completely perfect doctrine of the Sage;
without falling into sectarianism, you became the crown jewel
of all the tenet systems; I supplicate you. {443}

With rejecting harm to others as a basis, you practiced restraint;
with helping others as a basis, you endeavored in the training precepts;
and with clarity in the two phases of every visualization description,
you were thus a threefold vajra holder, I supplicate you.

You relied on many learned adepts, guides, and tutors;{445}
with diligence and noble motivation you plunged into the ocean of Sutra and Tantra;
and with the fine gifts of the jewels of classic and esoteric instructions,
you relieved the poverty of fortunate ones; I supplicate you.

Son of the Victor, you became father of all victors;
renouncing existence and quiescence, you are lord of all existence and quiescence;
glorious Cakrasaṃvara in the guise of a lama—
Drolwai Gönpo, I supplicate at your feet.

Heruka entrusted you with a treasury of secrets;
the Sage authorized you as the master of all dharma;
the eight bodhisattvas blessed you as the source
of all Sutra and Tantra; I bow in homage.

Avalokita praised you as a bodhisattva guide of beings;
Ākāśagarbha gave you the higher trainings;
Exalted Tārā continuously appeared and prophesied, {454}
raising your awareness; I bow in homage.

Padmākara inducted you into the circle of blood drinkers;
Yeshe Tsogyal conferred empowerment by profound symbols;
Ḍombī Heruka empowered you as the lord of the ḍākinīs
of the three places; I bow in homage.

Candragomin introduced you to meditative absorption;
Ārya[deva] washed away your pain during illness;
Goddess Sarasvatī granted you the power of eloquence—
to your unimaginably vast awareness, I bow in homage.

[Ḍākinī] Guhyajñānā conferred four secret empowerments;
ḍākinīs actually granted you all-conquering excellent medicine;
at Devīkoṭi, the Ḍākinī’s directives openly displayed[3]
the Six Dharmas; I bow in homage.

Luhipāda introduced you to great bliss;
you enjoyed the feast gatherings in the three circles;
you received prophecy that all who saw, heard, recalled, or touched you
on passion’s great path would be liberated; I bow in homage.

Rainbows and flowers appeared when you performed great deeds,
such as conferring empowerments, offering rituals, and teaching;
ḍākinīs’ symbolic songs and fragrances pervaded throughout {455}
as miraculous apparitions manifested; I bow in homage.

Ema! How wonderful this self-manifestation.
Rest in its native state, yogin.
Here, do not contrive anything at all;
the uncontrived is dharmakāya itself. {472}

Emaho!
If you want to meditate on the innate abiding nature,
no need to calculate the seasons, stars, and constellations;
when you remember the king of time, the time is right!
Don’t seek for a remote mountain retreat;
this mountain of your body is the best hermitage.

Don’t purposefully reject distractions;
knowing the variety as mind will be an ally,
like the grasses in a forest fire.
Don’t set retreat boundaries or create registers;
keeping silent is the best retreat.
Rest relaxed like a tuft of cotton wool.

That is the meaning of the nondual;
the suchness of the deity has no intrinsic nature.
After you meditate on compassion in that way, {475}
the unimaginable thought is to be of benefit; think in that way.

I pleased them and received their ultimate instructions. {478}
I resolved my misconceptions and did focused practice,
by which I attained both supreme and common spiritual powers.[15]

For that teaching you offered rare jewels and gold dust;
with palms together, you did full prostrations
and placed the bottom of my feet on your head.

To recognize that suchness of mind
and the vajra of conceptual mind itself;
that is the Vajra Ḍākinī guarding against obstacles.
Contentment with no needs is a precious gift;
that is the Jewel Ḍākinī accomplishing needs and desires.

The lotus of nonconceptual freedom from attachment;
that is the Lotus Ḍākinī gathering the mudras.
Karma without arising or ceasing;
that is the Activity Ḍākinī accomplishing actions.

Don’t they say that the lineage-holding gurus
are people endowed with three characteristics?
Adding instructions to that is a great ornament. {499}

Mind! Mind! Wander aimlessly begging for alms.
When you have wandered aimlessly begging for alms,
it’s like snow falling on a lake;
discursive thoughts dissolve instantly. {500}

The small bird of awareness in the branches
will get inspiration from the death-lord devil. {502}
You will go wherever your former actions take you;
to perform negative acts is pointless.

This is the prattle of a madman. {508}
I don’t ask for anyone’s pardon.
I have nothing to offer by way of apology.

Incomparable Kyergangpa
recognized form and sound as illusion.
Unattached, he helped beings through a deity’s form;
a dharma lord, in essence the three kāyas. {509}

The habitual body is the Victor’s kāya;
it accomplishes all purpose by thought alone. {510}
I am a wanderer in this illusory body with no reference.
The guru of my own mind taught me that.

If you don’t evoke compassion with torma and feast
from the dharma protector’s clouds of activity,
the rain of actions won’t fall.
Apply yourself to torma and feast, yogin! {514}

Reflect on death and impermanence constantly;
without any needs, you’ll abandon this life.
Your body can accomplish the two purposes in years or months;
meditate constantly on empty appearance without attachment as the deity’s form.

14. The mount of consciousness is karmic winds;
binding them through the application of yogic exercise
brings channels, winds, and drops under control;
bless me to accomplish Immortal Body.

18. From now until I attain buddhahood,
may I never be apart from you, Lord,
and accomplish whatever pleases you;
bless me in this path of meditation. {529}

Great Vajradhara in the form of an adept,
just hearing your name is meaningful.
Please turn my disciple’s mind to the dharma;
I supplicate you, a treasure of compassion. {531}

Rest in equipoise of your inseparable minds;
how could you prevent meditation from arising?
The desire for happiness by hoarding food and clothes
is a tremendous distraction from virtuous practice. {532}

Again, enhance virtuous practice with attributes;
it’s all the shifting display of mahāmudrā.
To perfect the two accumulations of method and wisdom
is to realize the intention of the buddhas. {533}

Don’t lose your hold on compassion
and leave it in nihilistic emptiness:
it’s important to practice them in union. {535}

First, these ever-changing four seasons;
second, these pictures of rising and falling prosperity;
third, these grave changes in the land and country:
these are the same teacher showing impermanence of the conditioned.

First, this farming that never ends;
second, these mean, ungrateful responses to care;
third, the salt water that doesn’t quench when drunk:
these are the same teacher who shows us futility in action.

First, this seething bustle of the village; {538}
second, this busy-bee activity of insignificant toil;
third, these wispy white clouds that flex and roil:
these are the same introduction showing aimless samsara.

First, this rainbow of formless appearance;
second, this clear echo without locality;
third, this unreal dream that produces joy or pain:
these are the same teacher who shows appearance as mind.

First, the magical machinations of outer appearances;
second, the doors of perception of inner mental awareness;
third, the emptiness of basic space without identity:
these are the same inseparability of pouring water into water.

The name of this is Purifying Inner Space,
the vitally important preliminary practice.
The support is the vajra body, channels, and vital-essence motion;
the basis of vital importance is the four chakras;
now blazing, melting, and four ecstasies move in the body:
this is the vitally important definitive secret of the tantras.

The condition is the meeting of method and wisdom;
the basis is introduction to one’s native mind; {541}
the support is the fall and rise of the four ecstasies:
that is the karma[mudrā] of Fierce Inner Heat.

The basis is to see your own original face;
the condition is intense longing devotion;
the vital point is to make the link of wind-mind united,
by which mind [is known as] vajra nature, great Lucid Clarity.

In the inseparability of the guru and the yidam, {543}
that yidam is one with the self-arising of illusion.
It is the radiance of relaxed uncontrived self-arising;
the guidance of impartial pure perception.

The path of channels is to have the vajra features;
the vital points are constraining and yogic exercises.
The path of vital winds is to retain the controlled breath in the vase;
the sublime vital point is fourfold breathing application.[75]

The path of vital drops is the flight and chase of melting bliss of A-haṃ;
the vital point is binding in the four chakras.
The path of Illusory Body is to see empty appearance as the deity’s form;
the vital point is to manifest as emanation without attachment.

The path of Dream is control through intentionality at sleep;
the vital point is to maintain the unborn when awake.
The path of Lucid Clarity is to gather the environment and inhabitants in luminosity;
the vital point is to bind wind and mind in balance.

The path of Intermediate State is to recall the threefold nature of phenomena;
the vital point is to always see the delusion.
The path of Transference is to eject the essence through the crown aperture;
the vital point is to gather and block the wind-mind.

For others, in accord with whatever experience occurs, {550}
taming by the vital points of winds, mind, and drops
supports the arising of unimaginable lucid clarity.

The lineage of Seven Jewels beginning with Great Vajradhara;
the golden rosary of bodhisattvas in their final lives, nonhumans assuming human form; {552}
and my glorious root guru who grants naked awakening:
I bow at your lotus feet—increase my experience and realization.

May longevity and merit increase,
and glory and wealth expand,
so that my renown equals the sky. {558}

It delights benevolent protectors, generates resplendent brilliance,
and discourages malevolent ones by dousing them with the elixir of awakening mind.
The energy of experience is created, and realization enhanced;
the seed of freedom is sown in those with faith. {559}

His curled tongue twitches in his gaping mouth as he laughs fiercely;
his tawny eyebrows, whiskers, and hair swirl upward;
he has a vermilion drop; and is crowned by King Akṣobhya.

To the left, from hūṃ, is black devil lord Trakṣad,
holding a lance banner and skull cup, riding a white-heeled black horse,
wearing devils’ garb, surrounded by an army of gods and devils. {597}

In apparent existence, all are your slaves;
in the three existences, all are your retinue;
and all arrogant spirits are your workers.
Quick as lightning, instantly you cover the universe
and reduce hateful enemies and harmful obstructors to dust.

Heart-blood arghaṃ; poisonous washing water;
sense organ flowers; burning-corpse incense;
lamps of human fat; perfume of blood, bile, and fat—
Awareness Protector and retinue, may sacred pledge be fulfilled.

Skull drums, thighbone trumpets, marching bands, majestic melodies;
fumes of burnt frankincense, human flesh, and mustard;
black silk banners and human-skin flags—
Awareness Protector and retinue, may sacred pledge be fulfilled.

Creation-phase deity meditation, paintings, and statues: the awakened body supports; {607}
winds, mantra recitation, life-force chakra: the awakened speech supports;
mudras, absorptions, insignia: the awakened mind supports—
Awareness Protector and retinue, may sacred pledge be fulfilled.

Ox hide, tiger skin, human skin, and animal hide;
skull necklaces, garlands, and six symbolic ornaments;
clusters of snakes, and vermilion ointment—
Awareness Protector and retinue, may sacred pledge be fulfilled.

Blazing and dripping of great bliss within samsara and nirvana;
the self-arising of unembellished lucid clarity as the deity’s form;
supreme mahāmudrā and eight common spiritual powers—
Awareness Protector and retinue, may sacred pledge be fulfilled.

Protect dharma centers, retreats, yogins, and their retinues;
dispel all outer, inner, and secret adverse conditions;
repel obstacles to the attainment of awakening;
and give refuge from the fears in this life, the next, and in between.

You are voracious and brilliant with thick limbs,
wrathful sounds of hūṃ resounding like thunder;
majestic as Meru, the color of eye medicine.

The inexhaustible blazing purity of your mind
is free of elaboration yet displays any characteristic. {616}
I praise you in terms of awakened body, speech, and mind.

Your terrifying gaping mouth bares fangs and curled tongue
while your laughter of a la la reverberates like thunder,
shaking the hosts of bhūtas in the vast universe.
I pay homage and praise you, terrifying goddess. {618}

To traverse the three-thousand fold universe, you ride a three-legged mule;
the front of the saddle is a rākṣasa’s upper jaw with a scored stick attached,
on which there are notches for enemies and obstructors.

Do the visualization for the wrathful recitation: {637}
oṃ śrī mahākāla śāsana / upahāriṇi / eṣo ’paścima kālo ayaṃ idaṃ ratna trayāya / apakāriṇaṃ yadi pratijñāṃ / smarasi tāda / idaṃ duṣṭaṃ kha kha khāhi khāhi / māra māra / gṛhṇa gṛhṇa / bandha bandha / hana hana / daha daha / paca paca / dinamekena māraya hūṃ phaṭ
This wrathful mantra is held to include the three [injunctions to] call, curse, and kill.

Qualities fully perfected like the snow mountains,
from which blessing rivers quench fortunate disciples,
you who reveal my mind as coemergence;
may there be auspiciousness of the sublime gurus, dharma sovereigns.

May merit rise like the sovereign Supreme Mountain,
great acclaim pervade everywhere like the sky,
and long life, health, and others’ welfare be spontaneously present;
may there be auspiciousness of a supreme ocean of qualities. {656}

Again, the flowers…(consecrate them as the mantra strings). Tossing them to you, imagine that you have the ability and power of mantra. {681}
Bhagavat, surely grant to these [disciples],
and please adhere to them. (Repeat three times.)

That purifies all verbal sickness, spirits, negativities, obscurations, and violations of sacred pledge accumulated in your lives of beginningless cycle existence. You become inseparable from the awakened speech of the guru and Protector.
Again, a blue letter hūṃ along with blue light rays of the hundred syllables emerge from the guru’s and Protector’s hearts. They come over and dissolve into your heart. Your heart inside is all filled with blue hūṃ letters and blue light rays of the hundred syllables. Think that you have obtained the mind blessing of both the guru and Protector. {698}
Say that and do the hundred syllables with music, and so on.

Guru-Protector’s vermilion mantras
with the color of overpowering
protectors, heroes, and ḍākinīs;
this supreme vital point of magnetizing
will bring supreme attainment now and in the future.
Keep this single lineage as if it were your life. {700}

de (708) ltar gsol ba btab pas bla ma'i thugs ka'i hU~M las 'od zer 'phros/ gtor ma mgon por gsal ba'i thugs kar phog pas thugs rgyud bskul te de'i mgrin pa'i AHlas kyang 'od zer 'phros/ phyogs bcu'i sangs rgyas byang sems thams cad kyi gsung gi byin rlabs thams cad dang / khyad par du yang mgon po'i gsung gi byin rlabs thams cad 'od zer gyi rnam par spyan drangs AHla thim/ de las bdud rtsi mchin kha'i rgyun babs/ slob ma'i mgrin pa nas zhugs mgrin pa longs spyod kyi 'khor lo khrig mer gyis gang bas ngag gi nad gdon sdig sgrib thams cad sangs kyis dag /
gsang ba'i dbang thob/ ye shes mgon po'i gsung gi byin rlabs thob pa'i mos pa mdzod {byas la}
DA dril dang sngags brjod/

de ltar gsol ba btab pas bla ma'i thugs ka'i hU~M las 'od zer 'phros/ gtor ma mgon por gsal ba'i thugs kar phog pas thugs rgyud bskul te de'i thugs ka'i hU~M las kyang 'od zer 'phros/ phyogs bcu'i sangs rgyas byang sems thams cad kyi thugs kyi byin rlabs thams cad dang / khyad par du yang mgon po'i thugs kyi byin rlabs thams cad 'od zer gyi rnam par spyan drangs hU~M la thim pas/ de las bdud rtsi mchin kha'i rgyun babs/ slob ma'i snying ga nas zhugs/ snying ga chos kyi 'khor lo khrig mer gyis gang bas yid kyi nad gdon sdig sgrib thams cad sangs kyis dag /
shes rab ye shes kyi dbang thob/ ye shes mgon po'i thugs kyi byin rlabs thob pa'i mos pa mdzod/ (709) {byas la}
DA dril dang bcas pas sngags brjod/

de ltar gsol ba btab pas bla ma'i thugs ka'i hU~M las 'od zer 'phros/ gtor ma mgon por gsal ba'i thugs kar phog pas thugs rgyud bskul te/ de'i gnas gsum gyi yig 'bru gsum las 'od zer 'phros/ phyogs bcu'i sangs rgyas byang sems thams cad kyi sku gsung thugs yon tan phrin las dang bcas pa'i byin rlabs thams cad 'od zer gyi rnam par spyan drangs/ mgon po'i gnas gsum gyi yi ge gsum la thim/ de las bdud rtsi'i rgyun babs/ spyi bo nas rkang mthil gyi bar du gang bas lus ngag yid gsum gyi sdig sgrib thams cad skad cig nyid la sangs kyis dag /
tshig dbang rin po che thob/ ye shes mgon po'i sku gsung thugs yon tan phrin las dang bcas pa'i byin rlabs thob pa'i mos pa mdzod {byas la}
sngags brjod/

Put the disciples’ flowers on their heads. {710}
Bhagavat, surely grant to these [disciples],
and please adhere to them. (Repeat three times.)

Then for the completely perfect blessings, do this visualization of the torma’s exhortation: This torma itself is Swift-Acting Awareness Protector…(etc.).
Continue as in Removing All Obstacles, except that during the guru lineage supplication, change to:
Pervasive Lord Great Vajradhara, great brahmin Saraha, mighty glorious Śavarīpa…(etc. to)…Chöje Sangye Tönpa…(etc. to)…up to my root guru—all these glorious holy gurus…(etc.). {717}

Recite the root mantra and offer incense and music. Apply [to this the following]: {721}
That was the authorization of awakened body. Again light rays radiate from hūṃ in the guru’s heart. They strike the torma appearing as Protector and evoke his mind stream. From his heart, infinite light rays radiate and invoke all the speech blessings of all tathāgatas and victors’ heirs from the ten directions in the forms of countless big and small bodies of the principals and retinue. They dissolve into the disciples’ throats and fill their whole bodies with deity bodies and light rays. Based on that, all verbal negativities, obscurations, and obstacles are purified. Imagine that you have obtained the Protector’s blessings of awakened speech.
Say the root mantra while offering incense and music.

Light rays from the heart of Guru Vajradhara on your heads invoke the four deities—Avalokita to the guru’s crown, Tārā to the throat, Protector to the heart, and Yoginī to the navel. With devotion to those deities dwelling there, repeat this after me:
“namo buddhāya…(etc. to)…ture svāhā”
Repeat the set of five mantras three times. {732}

Arise! Arise! Arise from the realm of phenomena.
Without moving from within the pure phenomenal realm,
you display the wrathful form to subdue the wicked: {761}

Tapping your toenail on the ground, the earth quakes;
uttering hūṃ, the mountains crack and the oceans heave;
a wink of your eye banishes all obstacles:
powerful one of unrestrained might—power to you!
